---
/*
 * The full personal-capacity note. Lives in one component so the short line in
 * the hero and this expanded version can never drift apart.
 *
 * NOT legally reviewed — see PLAN.md open questions.
 */
---

<section class="disclaimer" id="disclaimer" aria-labelledby="disclaimer-title">
  <div class="disclaimer__inner">
    <h2 class="disclaimer__title" id="disclaimer-title">A note on what you read here</h2>
    <p>
      Everything on this site is written in a personal capacity. The opinions, analyses and
      conclusions are my own, formed in my own time, and do not represent the positions of my
      employer or of any organisation I work with. Nothing here should be read as a statement on
      their behalf.
    </p>
    <p>
      Academic publications are the one exception. Those were carried out and published under the
      institute named on each paper, and that work stands on its own terms — it is listed here for
      reference, with any commentary I add around it being, again, my own view rather than the
      institute’s.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /*
   * The divider spans the full width, matching the other section dividers on
   * the landing page; the text sits in a centered, measure-width column
   * inside it — a centered block, not centered text, since centering
   * multi-line prose itself would ragged the line ends.
   */
  .disclaimer {
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--text-1);
  }

  .disclaimer__inner {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-inline: auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .disclaimer__title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-0);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
